# Real, current (non-deprecated) ArduPilot hardening -- verified live
# 2026-08-08 against this exact vehicle, both mechanisms independently:
#
# GPS1_TYPE 14: switches the GPS driver to AP_GPS_MAV (external MAVLink
# GPS_INPUT), so GPS becomes just another sensor the EKF fuses and
# cross-checks against the real Gazebo-physics-derived IMU -- rather than
# GPS being embedded in the same JSON FDM feed the IMU is also derived
# from (which is why a vehicle WITHOUT this set has no independent signal
# to catch a spoof against at all). Verified: a step GPS_INPUT spoof after
# this is set results in the fused belief moving 0.00m while raw ingestion
# confirms the forged value reached the wire at the full offset -- the EKF
# is seeing and rejecting it, not simply not receiving it.
#
# MAV_GCS_SYSID 77 + MAV_OPTIONS 1 (bit 0 = GCS_SYSID_ENFORCE): the modern
# replacement for the deprecated SYSID_MYGCS mechanism (confirmed in this
# ArduPilot source tree: SYSID_MYGCS is commented "unused" in this version).
# With enforcement OFF (the default on every unhardened vehicle in this
# project), ArduPilot's accept_packet() fails OPEN -- any sender is
# accepted regardless of MAV_GCS_SYSID. Only with MAV_OPTIONS bit 0 set
# does it actually reject senders that don't match MAV_GCS_SYSID. Verified
# live: source_system=255 (this project's attacker-simulation default,
# also ArduPilot's own out-of-the-box default) gets rejected outright --
# can't even arm -- while source_system=77 (this project's own legitimate
# tooling, see constants.GCS_SOURCE_SYSTEM) arms and controls normally.
GPS1_TYPE 14
MAV_GCS_SYSID 77
MAV_OPTIONS 1
